{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/581847-short-questions-about-the-game","id":581847,"title":"Short questions about the game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-06T19:58:23-07:00","id":581847,"title":"Short questions about the game","content":"I've been looking over reviews for this game and came upon a lengthy one that made a point of it being a hard game to GM. So in effect I ask the community if Mummy is harder to GM than any other WoD game out there? I realize there will be a special approach to it, like most WoD games have, but is it actually harder?<br /> <br /> I came to be interested with this game because of my love for the ancient Near East cultures so I'm thrilled with a game that takes some inspiration from that direction. But I wouldn't want to buy it, run it and find its really not my type of game at all, after the money, time and energy are already spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:11:38-07:00","id":581890,"title":"","content":"Hm. Not sure about &quot;harder&quot;. To a certain extent I think that depends upon the structure. If you're running a game in multiple time lines, either simultaneously or as a progression through time, then that could be a lot of content you need to develop. With a &quot;normal&quot; chronicle, it doesn't feel like all that much extra work.<br /> <br /> The big pieces of extra work for the GM come from the player characters, specifically. They are going to have a very limited understanding of their own backstory from the get-go, and it's up to you to provide it in the course of play. So you'll need some detailed notes on who the characters are and what they've been doing for the last 6,000 years. It probably helps if you can tie their history into the events of your game and antagonists/other NPCs. That, I think, is where most of the work is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:41:49-07:00","id":581908,"title":"","content":"The main issue that gives STs pause, I think, is the nature of the Descent. Most mummies exist in a cycle where they first rise in the world for a specific purpose. They begin their cycle with the ability to bring tremendous supernatural force to bear \u2014 potentially we're talking crater a city power, depending on which Utterances the character starts with \u2014 and then over time it wanes until it gutters out and ends the cycle, and the mummy falls dead once again. At that point, a return to life and the beginning of a new cycle is entirely dependent on circumstance, and could be anything from a matter of months to a matter of centuries. (Notably, there is one circumstance approximately every 1500 years when all mummies arise. That's a special cycle where time can bring your supernatural force low but can't gutter it out entirely. Other circumstances, such as being killed or breaking certain taboos, can still end that cycle.)<br /> <br /> In addition to that, there's some emphasis on mummies acting through servitor cults they've raised through the ages, and a lot of emphasis on hidden knowledge. Mummies work to clear their Memory, and it's assumed that characters' backstories won't be set ahead of time by the players, but will emerge through play as their Memory increases and they encounter evidence of their own past.<br /> <br /> So, cycles of life that potentially could have long intervals between them; power overwhelming to be had early but waning over time; a murky backstory where your characters remember little of what the holy traditions they labor to honor and maintain were like in life. If that sounds like something you can work with, then you're probably set. If it sounds like a setup you'd have difficulty with, you might hold back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 07-06-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T21:17:10-07:00","id":581926,"title":"","content":"From the sound of it, it sounds like its should be managable. God knows that I am love to make detailed character backgrounds and goals, only to find the characters horrifically butchered in swift order, so the Descent shouldn't be to difficult for me. <br /> <br /> I shall invest my hard-earned cash and see if my group likes the taste of it. And if not I can save it for later.<br /> <br /> Thanks guys for the info about the game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T23:03:10-07:00","id":585682,"title":"","content":"That is one nice thing about Mummy - you really don't have to worry about killing your players. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T23:09:31-07:00","id":585687,"title":"","content":"Just, um, don't get too carried away.<br /> <br /> *has killed one player five times*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:36:16-07:00","id":585729,"title":"","content":"One of the many odd perks of the gameline. You can give a PC a dramatic death scene, and still have him return later on (with a kewl story on how they got the body back.). Ive found it easier to come up with plot hooks for this than Demon oddly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T20:02:19-07:00","id":586720,"title":"","content":"Well, it does have the built in all-purpose plot hook of &quot;Reeeelic... Mummy get! Rarrr!&quot; :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}